From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Restore USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE on USB4
 exit

While the USB4 router owns the Glymur combo PHY, its firmware takes the
USB4 PCS reset out of always-on hardware control by clearing
USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE, and leaves it cleared when it releases the PHY.
The always-on block keeps that setting across a CX power collapse.
After the next system sleep the native USB3 PHY on the port no longer
comes out of reset ("phy initialization timed-out") until the machine
is rebooted.

Set USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE again, its reset value, when the USB4 PHY is
released and before the common block is powered down.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index a754f46929c..bd54fa063fd 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -120,6 +120,7 @@ enum qphy_reg_layout {
 
 	QPHY_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE,
 	QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE,
+	QPHY_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE,
 	/* Keep last to ensure regs_layout arrays are properly initialized */
 	QPHY_LAYOUT_SIZE
 };
@@ -326,6 +327,7 @@ static const unsigned int qmp_v8_n3_usb43dpphy_regs_layout[QPHY_LAYOUT_SIZE] = {
 	[QPHY_PCS_USB4_CLAMP_ENABLE]		= QPHY_V8_PCS_AON_USB4_AON_CLAMP_ENABLE,
 	[QPHY_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE]		= QPHY_V8_PCS_AON_USB3_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE,
 	[QPHY_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE]		= QPHY_V8_PCS_AON_DP_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE,
+	[QPHY_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE]		= QPHY_V8_PCS_AON_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE,
 
 	[QPHY_COM_RESETSM_CNTRL]		= QSERDES_V8_COM_RESETSM_CNTRL,
 	[QPHY_COM_C_READY_STATUS]		= DP_QSERDES_V8_COM_C_READY_STATUS,
@@ -4979,6 +4981,17 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb4_exit(struct phy *phy)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The router firmware takes the USB4 PCS reset out of always-on
+	 * hardware control while it owns the PHY and leaves it that way. The
+	 * always-on block keeps the setting across a CX power collapse, after
+	 * which the native USB3 PHY no longer comes out of reset ("phy
+	 * initialization timed-out") until the next boot. Hand the USB4 PCS
+	 * back to hardware control, its reset value, while the PHY is powered.
+	 */
+	if (qmp->pcs_aon && qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE])
+		qphy_setbits(qmp->pcs_aon, qmp->cfg->regs[QPHY_USB4_AON_TOGGLE_ENABLE], 0x1);
+
 	ret = qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, false);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-- 
